Clawblox: never download esbuild at run time (no `npx --yes esbuild` fallback); use a pinned one

Applies to: Clawblox (https://github.com/nacloos/clawblox) at commit 8be90a0, on its own or after the
other ten; apply all eleven in the order of the README's table.
Clawblox is MIT-licensed (see worlds/beach/renderer/LICENSE.clawblox); this patch changes a few
lines of its code and is offered under the same MIT terms. Written for AI Beach.

    git apply /path/to/AI-Beach/patches/clawblox-no-npx-esbuild.patch
    cargo build --release

Why (a security review, 10-21): each time a world starts, Clawblox bundles its renderer with esbuild.
When no `esbuild` program was found on PATH, it ran `npx --yes esbuild`, which fetches whatever esbuild
is newest from the npm registry and runs it with the world's account: unpinned code from the internet,
at every start, without anyone choosing it. On Windows this was the usual path, because a global
`npm install -g esbuild` makes only an `esbuild.cmd` shim, which Clawblox's program check doesn't run.

What changes: Clawblox uses the esbuild named by the CLAWBLOX_ESBUILD environment variable (a full path,
for a pinned copy), or `esbuild` on PATH. If neither runs, the world stops with a message that says how
to install one, instead of downloading anything. AI Beach's launcher sets CLAWBLOX_ESBUILD from its
`--esbuild` option (or AI_BEACH_ESBUILD). On Windows, point it at the native program inside the npm
package: node_modules/@esbuild/win32-x64/esbuild.exe.

diff --git a/src/bin/cli.rs b/src/bin/cli.rs
--- a/src/bin/cli.rs
+++ b/src/bin/cli.rs
@@ -1628,23 +1628,21 @@ fn bundle_renderer_with_esbuild(
         )
     })?;
 
-    let mut needs_npm_cache = false;
-    let mut cmd = if command_exists("esbuild") {
-        let mut c = Command::new("esbuild");
-        c.arg(source.as_os_str());
-        c
-    } else if command_exists("npx") {
-        needs_npm_cache = true;
-        let mut c = Command::new("npx");
-        c.args(["--yes", "esbuild"]);
-        c.arg(source.as_os_str());
-        c
-    } else {
-        return Err(
-            "Could not find esbuild or npx in PATH. Install esbuild (npm i -D esbuild) or Node.js."
-                .to_string(),
-        );
-    };
+    // AI Beach: never fetch esbuild at run time. The old fallback ran `npx --yes esbuild`, which downloads
+    // whatever esbuild is newest from the npm registry each time a world starts: unpinned code, run with
+    // the world's account. Use the esbuild named by CLAWBLOX_ESBUILD (a full path, for a pinned copy), or
+    // one on PATH; otherwise stop and say how to install one.
+    let esbuild = std::env::var("CLAWBLOX_ESBUILD").unwrap_or_else(|_| "esbuild".to_string());
+    if !command_exists(&esbuild) {
+        return Err(format!(
+            "Could not run esbuild ({}). Install esbuild 0.28.2 and set CLAWBLOX_ESBUILD to the program's full \
+             path (on Windows, the esbuild.exe inside node_modules/@esbuild/win32-x64; npm's esbuild.cmd can't be \
+             run). On macOS and Linux, an esbuild on PATH also works. This engine no longer downloads esbuild with npx.",
+            esbuild
+        ));
+    }
+    let mut cmd = Command::new(&esbuild);
+    cmd.arg(source.as_os_str());
 
     cmd.current_dir(game_dir).args([
         "--bundle",
@@ -1655,18 +1653,6 @@ fn bundle_renderer_with_esbuild(
         "--log-level=warning",
     ]);
 
-    if needs_npm_cache {
-        let npm_cache_dir = std::env::temp_dir().join("clawblox-npm-cache");
-        std::fs::create_dir_all(&npm_cache_dir).map_err(|e| {
-            format!(
-                "Failed to create npm cache dir {}: {}",
-                npm_cache_dir.display(),
-                e
-            )
-        })?;
-        cmd.env("NPM_CONFIG_CACHE", &npm_cache_dir);
-    }
-
     let output = cmd
         .arg(format!("--outfile={}", out.display()))
         .output()
